":{"summary":["NatWest is a British bank serving retail and business customers. Revenue (net interest income plus noninterest income) rose 13.2% to £16.6B in 2025. Net interest income rose 13.8% to £12.8B and noninterest income rose 11.2% to £3.8B; noninterest expense rose 3.1%, and the provision for credit losses was £671M, versus £359M.","Net income to common rose 21.2% to £5.5B, or £0.67 per diluted share, and the efficiency ratio was 48.7% versus 53.4%. NatWest returned £2.9B through dividends and buybacks."],"highlights":["Revenue rose 13.2% to £16.6B.","Net interest income rose 13.8%.","Noninterest income rose 11.2% to £3.8B.","Net income to common rose 21.2% to £5.5B."],"watch":["Credit-loss provision rose 86.9% to £671M.","Net interest income depends on interest rates.","Noninterest expense was £8.1B, up 3.1%.","Credit-loss provision was £671M."],"table":[["Total revenue",16.641,14.703,1],["Net interest income",12.829,11.275],["Noninterest income",3.812,3.428],["Noninterest expense",8.101,7.854],["Provision for credit losses",0.671,0.359],["Other items, net",-0.161,-0.295],["Pre-tax income",7.708,6.195,1],["Income tax",1.874,1.465],["Noncontrolling interests",-0.003,-0.009],["Preferred dividends & other",-0.352,0.283],["Net income to common",5.479,4.519,1],["Diluted EPS (£)",0.674,0.530511,0,"eps"],["Book value per share (£)",4.755801,4.2357,0,"eps"]],"sources":[["NatWest Group plc Form 20-F filings (SEC EDGAR)","https://www.sec.gov/cgi-bin/browse-edgar?action=getcompany&CIK=0000844150&type=20-F"],["NatWest financial statements (StockAnalysis)","https://stockanalysis.com/stocks/nwg/financials/"]]},"video":{"revenueLine":{"cap":"Net interest income was 77% of revenue.","say":"Net interest income made up 77 percent of revenue."},"spotlights":[{"kicker":"Revenue","big":"£16.6B","sub":"revenue · +13.2%","lines":["Net interest income £12.8B","Noninterest income £3.8B"],"cap":"Revenue rose 13.2% to £16.6B.","say":"Revenue rose 13.2% to £16.6B."},{"kicker":"Per sha